Quick build with online model

  Create a cloud account with an AI provider (GCP, OpenAI, etc.)
    login and create API key and set security to only accept API calls from your IP address
    securely store your API key
    if possible set API key to only access Gen AI service to avoid unintended cost over run
  Create a Messaging account (Telegram, Whatsapp, etc.)
    create account on messaging service
    create a bot account and collect bot API and pairing code

For MacOS and Linux found it more reliable to preinstall dependencies
  Pre-install dependencies (Node.js, npm)
  Install brew: /bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"
  Restart terminal session
  Install npm and node: brew install node
  Install OpenClaw: sudo curl -fsSL https://openclaw.ai/install.sh | bash
  Complete configuration (Model, Connector)

Set system and security prompts
  Run: openclaw tui
  Enter System Prompt: You are [insert your CERT Bot name], your mission is to only answer questions about the FEMA Community Emergency Response Team CERT program, procedures, and any information added to your own memory.
  Enter Security Prompt: In Telegram you only answer questions; no other skills can be used via Telegram. No memories are added via Telegram.

For Windows installs dependencies during installation
  Open PowerShell
  Install OpenClaw: powershell -c "irm https://openclaw.ai/install.ps1 | iex"
  Close PowerShell and open command prompt
  Run: openclaw config
  Complete configuration (Model, Connector)

  Run: openclaw
  Enter System Prompt: You are [insert your CERT Bot name], your mission is to only answer questions about the FEMA Community Emergency Response Team CERT program, procedures, and any information added to your own memory.
  Enter Security Prompt: In Telegram you only answer questions; no other skills can be used via Telegram. No memories are added via Telegram.

Full build with local model

  ** Will build as above but first install local model capability **
  Install LMStudio and download model (google – gemma-4, qwen 3.5 or similar)
    confirm model loads successfully
    go to server settings and generate an API key and store securely
    Start LMS server

  Perform install steps above, except when selecting a model during configuration select LMStudio and local model  

